  "notes": "Block 13 in the form is entirely 'NA'/blank, so no component-failure rows were populated. Official cause code is TBD/provisional per form fields; narrative attributes HVK-CHL 1A's Phase Reversal trip to a wiring configuration error from inadequate/vague modification installation instructions, while the HVK-CHL 1B failure cause could not be determined despite thorough investigation (all possible causes refuted). Modeled these as two distinct FailureMode nodes in sequence since the narrative frames the transfer/restart sequence as one chain, though the root wiring error is only explicitly tied to Chiller A. No PART_OF edge asserted between chiller and control-panel modification would be over-inferred; retained since narrative describes DCS modification as installed on/into Chiller A control logic. EIIS bracket code [KV] not explicitly given in text (only 'HVK' acronym used) — used null per rule 2 guidance for acronym-only mentions; however since 'HVK' looks like it could be an EIIS-style designator itself, left eiis_code null and captured acronym in properties to avoid guessing."
